+# smallpt browser studio
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The page runs the C++ integrator in a module Web Worker and transfers progressive RGBA frames to a canvas. Randomize changes the two sphere tints and the diffuse side walls. Reset restores the original scene. PNG downloads capture the current render.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten (`em++` on PATH), then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+The generated `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm` are checked in, so a static host can serve this directory without a build. Serve over HTTP(S) with `.wasm` mapped to `application/wasm` and JavaScript mapped to a JavaScript MIME type. No application backend, cross-origin isolation headers, or runtime compilation is required. Opening `index.html` through `file://` will not support module workers.
+
+`vendor/smallpt-original.cpp` retains the original source. `src/smallpt-core.hpp` contains its tracing core, with braces added around the Russian roulette conditional for warning-clean compilation. `src/renderer.cpp` adds a progressive 2×2 subpixel buffer and browser API. The 1 MB WebAssembly stack accommodates the recursive tracer. `assets/preview.png` is a 256-spp render made by compiling the same adapter natively, displayed until the first live frame arrives.
+
+Sample and resolution controls start a new render. Stop terminates the worker immediately. More samples reduce noise and take more CPU time. The original scene, ray/sphere intersection, diffuse/specular/dielectric materials, Russian roulette, and tent-filtered camera sampling are preserved. Colors and samples stay client-side. Google Fonts supplies optional interface typography with local sans-serif fallbacks.
+
+Original renderer © Kevin Beason, MIT license; see `vendor/LICENSE.txt`.
+
+Validation: release Emscripten build, JavaScript syntax checks, and a non-browser WebAssembly smoke check. No browser verification or dev/preview server was used.
